  "theHarnessDefect": {
    "whatProductionPersisted": "orgunit_page_evidence rows for genuine 2xx HTML responses with a resolvable charset whose extraction yielded zero characters. Legal, intended production evidence; persistPageEvidence does not reject an empty extraction, and that is not a bug.",
    "whatTheBridgeCounted": "every persisted page-evidence row entered SD7 deduplication. A zero-character main_text produces no token 5-grams, so the bridge recorded it SD7_SHORT_TEXT_UNRESOLVED and let it contribute 0..1 to the post-SD7 survivor count.",
    "whySd9ForbidsThat": "SD9 counts 'at least 4 distinct pages WITH EXTRACTABLE TEXT'. A page with zero extracted characters has no extractable text, so the upper end of that 0..1 contribution asserted something SD9's own wording excludes with certainty.",
    "repairedBy": "a branded eligibility gate that only partitionByExtractableText can mint, so no page row with main_text_chars = 0 can reach exact or near-duplicate deduplication by any route."
  },
